FUN_1000_140e: MEMMGR pool size = the DOS AH=48 max-alloc result, not a phantom register param.

140e (asm 0x1140e) grabs all available conventional memory and builds the MEMMGR pool over it:

    mov ah,0x48 ; mov bx,0xffff ; int 21h   ; query -> BX = largest free block (paragraphs)
    push bx ; mov ah,0x48 ; int 21h ; pop bx ; alloc that block  (-> AX = block segment)
    mov [0x1758],ax                          ; save block seg
    mov cx,0x300 ; call 0x11467              ; 1467(AX=block, CX=0x300 align, BX=size)

The size handed to 1467 is BX = the AH=48 query result (the whole free block, ~23552 paras here). The
__allregs decompiler cannot see that BX is produced by the INT 21h (the swi() intrinsic does not model
BX out), so it treated 1467's third argument as an incoming register PARAMETER (param_7) — which arrives
as garbage (99) from 06bc. Result: 1467 built a 99-paragraph pool inside the 23552-paragraph block, so
the first real request larger than ~85 paragraphs (e.g. the 356-para scratch buffer at FUN_0000_14da)
overflowed the pool -> 0a31 returned "out of memory" (CF=1) -> 184b panicked via 13e4. (Latent until
patch 025 made 0a31 actually run; before that it hung in the folded walk.)

Fix: pass the saved query result (uStack0002 = uRam000f0002 captured right after the query INT 21h =
the BX the asm forwards) as the pool size. The pool now spans the whole allocated block. Asm-verified
base-0 0x1140e..0x11429.
--- a/fist.c
+++ b/fist.c
@@ -39947,7 +39947,10 @@
   fist_int_dispatch();
   if (!(bool)uRam000f0012) {
     DAT_1000_d758 = uRam000f0000;
-    FUN_1000_1467(uRam000f0000,0x300,param_7);
+    /* PATCH 026: 1467's size = BX = the AH=48 query result (uStack0002), i.e. the whole free block,
+       NOT the phantom register param_7 (__allregs could not thread BX through the INT 21h). Asm
+       0x11429 calls 1467 with BX = the pushed/popped AH=48 max-alloc size. */
+    FUN_1000_1467(uRam000f0000,0x300,uStack0002);
     uVar3 = DAT_1000_d758;
     /* PATCH 014: rep movsw source segment restore (dropped far base on string op). Asm (0x1140e+0x1e):
          mov ax,ds; mov es,ax; mov di,0x16d4; mov ds,[0x1758]; xor si,si; mov cx,0x10; rep movsw
